<title>USA: CalEnergy completes private placement.</title>
<headline>CalEnergy completes private placement.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Neb. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>CalEnergy Co Inc said CalEnergy Capital Trust II, a special purpose Delaware business trust formed by the company, completed a $150 million private placement of trust convertible preferred securities.</p>
<p>It also said that Lehman Brothers and Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette exercised an option to buy an additional 600,000 trust securities, or $30 million in the aggregate, to cover overallotments.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used by CalEnergy, a provider of energy services, to fund ongoing construction expenses for its international projects and to pay down debt.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
